IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcr-dates`
IMPORT `wcr-earnings`

-- Workers Compensation Regulation 2016 (NSW) -- worked cases for Parts 3, 4 and 5 (wcr-earnings.l4). Every expected value
-- was worked by hand from the deposited text, with the day counts in comments; none was copied from the encoding's
-- output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- earnings and return to work assistance`

`d` MEANS `the calendar day`
`any day` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 1 2000

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE, c IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Earning period`
`the period` a b c e MEANS JUST (`Earning period` WITH
    `the first day of the period` IS a
    `the last day of the period` IS b
    `days excluded inside it` IS c
    `days that count` IS e)

§§ `cl 6, cl 8AB -- the $155 minimum`

#ASSERT `My PIAWE after the minimum` 120 EQUALS 155
#ASSERT `My PIAWE after the minimum` 155 EQUALS 155
#ASSERT `My PIAWE after the minimum` 155.01 EQUALS 155.01
#ASSERT `My PIAWE after the minimum` 900 EQUALS 900

§§ `cl 7 -- 38 hours, for injuries before 21 October 2019 only`

#ASSERT `The prescribed number of hours for my injury` (`d` 20 10 2019) EQUALS JUST 38
#ASSERT `The prescribed number of hours for my injury` (`d` 21 10 2019) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `cll 8A-8EA -- the relevant earning period`

-- Arguments: injury, first engaged, ongoing change, its day, unpaid leave, its first day, earnings payable again, COVID
-- change, material reduction 23 March-14 June 2020, first day from 15 June 2020 with earnings payable.

-- Injury 1 July 2024. The 52 weeks end 30 June 2024 and start 364 days before the injury: 1 July 2023 is 366 days
-- before (29 February 2024 lies between), so the start is 3 July 2023. 3 July 2023 to 30 June 2024 is 364 days.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 364
-- 52,000 over 364 days: 52,000 x 7 / 364 = 1,000 a week.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 52000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- 5,000 over 364 days is 96.15 a week: the $155 minimum applies.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 5000 EQUALS JUST 155

-- cl 8B: first engaged 1 January 2024: the period runs 1 January to 30 June 2024 = 31+29+31+30+31+30 = 182 days;
-- 26,000 x 7 / 182 = 1,000.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 182
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 26000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Engaged on the day of the injury: no day counts, so the Regulation's averaging gives no answer.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- cl 8C: a change to part-time on 1 April 2024: the period runs 1 April to 30 June 2024 = 30+31+30 = 91 days;
-- 9,100 x 7 / 91 = 700.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2024) FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 1 4 2024) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 91
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2024) FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 9100 EQUALS JUST 700
-- A change after the injury (5 July 2024) is not "during" the period.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 5 7 2024) FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 364
-- 8B then 8C: engaged 1 January 2024, change 1 March 2024: 1 March to 30 June = 31+30+31+30 = 122 days.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 122

-- cl 8E: unpaid leave from 1 February 2024, earnings payable again 15 February: 1-14 February excluded (14 days), 350
-- count; 35,000 x 7 / 350 = 700.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) (`d` 15 2 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 14 350
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) (`d` 15 2 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` 35000 EQUALS JUST 700
-- Exactly 7 days without earnings (1-7 February, payable again 8 February): excluded. 6 days (payable again 7 February):
-- "not less than seven consecutive calendar days" is not met, nothing excluded.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) (`d` 8 2 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 7 357
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) (`d` 7 2 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 364
-- Leave from 20 June 2024 still running at the injury: 20-30 June excluded (11 days).
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2024) (`d` 10 7 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 11 353
-- Leave that began before the period (25 June 2023) does not commence within it (fork F6): nothing excluded.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 25 6 2023) (`d` 20 7 2023) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the period` (`d` 3 7 2023) (`d` 30 6 2024) 0 364

-- cl 8EA. Injury 1 March 2021: the period ends 28 February 2021 and starts 364 days before the injury, 2 March 2020
-- (1 March 2020 is 365 days before). First prescribed period 23 March-14 June 2020: 9+30+31+14 = 84 days.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 6 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 84 280
-- No material reduction: nothing excluded.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 0 364
-- No earnings until 1 August 2020: 15 June-31 July also excluded, 16+31 = 47 days; 84+47 = 131.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 8 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 131 233
-- No earnings until 1 November 2020: capped at 27 September, 16+31+31+27 = 105 days; 84+105 = 189.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 11 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 189 175
-- "2 or more days": earnings again 16 June is 1 day (not excluded); 17 June is 2 days (15 and 16 June excluded).
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE (`d` 16 6 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 84 280
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE (`d` 17 6 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 86 278
-- Unpaid leave 1-30 June 2020 overlapping both prescribed periods, earnings again 1 July: the days excluded are
-- 23 March-30 June 2020 once each, 84 + 16 = 100.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 1 3 2021) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) (`d` 1 7 2020) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2020) EQUALS `the period` (`d` 2 3 2020) (`d` 28 2 2021) 100 264

-- Before 21 October 2019 Part 4 does not apply (cl 8(2)).
#ASSERT `What is my relevant earning period` (`d` 20 10 2019) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` (`d` 20 10 2019) (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE `any day` 52000 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `cl 8D -- alignment with the pay period`

#ASSERT `May my earning period be aligned with my pay` (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May my earning period be aligned with my pay` (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before 21 October 2019: Part 4 "applies only to injuries received on or after" that day (cl 8(2)).
#ASSERT `May my earning period be aligned with my pay` (`d` 1 7 2019) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `cl 8G -- apprentices, trainees and young people`

#ASSERT `My PIAWE as an apprentice, trainee or young worker` TRUE TRUE 1200 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1200
-- No comparable workers aged 21 or over: the maximum weekly compensation amount, $1,838.70 as deposited.
#ASSERT `My PIAWE as an apprentice, trainee or young worker` TRUE FALSE 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1838.70
#ASSERT `My PIAWE as an apprentice, trainee or young worker` TRUE FALSE 0 (JUST 2000) EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `My PIAWE as an apprentice, trainee or young worker` FALSE TRUE 1200 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `cll 8H-8M -- PIAWE agreements`

-- cl 8J(2): notified 10 March 2025, application by 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must our PIAWE agreement application be made` (`d` 10 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2025
-- Applied on day 5 (15 March): in time; day 6 (16 March): late.
#ASSERT `Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 16 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
-- Not yet applied: on 14 March and on 15 March still open; on 16 March missed.
#ASSERT `Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` (`d` 10 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 14 3 2025) EQUALS `the duty is still open and still in time`
#ASSERT `Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` (`d` 10 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `the duty is still open and still in time`
#ASSERT `Was our PIAWE agreement application made in time` (`d` 10 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 16 3 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`

-- cl 8K. Arguments: in time, age, patient, guardianship, protected, incommunicate, other incapacity, prior work capacity
-- decision, disputes liability, already approved, satisfied.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5) and (11)(a): a child under 18. At 18 the bar is gone.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8) an earlier work capacity decision about the PIAWE.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 8H(2) liability for weekly payments disputed.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 8L(1) only one agreement.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not satisfied the amount is fair.
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Late application (fork F8).
#ASSERT `Must the insurer approve our PIAWE agreement` FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- cl 8I: the agreed amount, never below $155; nothing once liability is disputed or a party withdraws.
#ASSERT `What PIAWE apply under our agreement` TRUE 1200 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `What PIAWE apply under our agreement` TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 155
#ASSERT `What PIAWE apply under our agreement` TRUE 1200 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What PIAWE apply under our agreement` TRUE 1200 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What PIAWE apply under our agreement` FALSE 1200 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- cl 8L(2): the benefit withdrawn "on or after the date of the injury".
#ASSERT `May the insurer approve a variation of our agreement` (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer approve a variation of our agreement` (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the insurer approve a variation of our agreement` (`d` 1 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- cl 8K(2): received 3 June 2025, decide by 10 June. (3): excuse ended 20 June, liability accepted 15 June: the earlier is
-- 15 June, decide by 22 June. Only the excuse ended (20 June): by 27 June. Neither yet: the 7 days have not started.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide our PIAWE agreement` (`d` 3 6 2025) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 6 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide our PIAWE agreement` (`d` 3 6 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (`d` 22 6 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide our PIAWE agreement` (`d` 3 6 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST (`d` 27 6 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide our PIAWE agreement` (`d` 3 6 2025) TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Decided on 10 June: in time; 11 June: late; not decided, today 9 June: still open.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` (`d` 3 6 2025) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 10 6 2025) (`d` 12 6 2025) EQUALS JUST `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` (`d` 3 6 2025) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 11 6 2025) (`d` 12 6 2025) EQUALS JUST `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` (`d` 3 6 2025) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 9 6 2025) EQUALS JUST `the duty is still open and still in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` (`d` 3 6 2025) TRUE FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) TRUE (`d` 22 6 2025) (`d` 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer decided our PIAWE agreement in time` (`d` 3 6 2025) TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 30 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- cl 8M(2): notice of withdrawal received 1 September 2025, act by 8 September.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer act on the withdrawal` (`d` 1 9 2025) EQUALS `d` 8 9 2025
#ASSERT `Has the insurer acted on the withdrawal in time` (`d` 1 9 2025) TRUE (`d` 8 9 2025) (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer acted on the withdrawal in time` (`d` 1 9 2025) TRUE (`d` 9 9 2025) (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer acted on the withdrawal in time` (`d` 1 9 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`

§§ `cl 8N -- payment increase decisions`

#ASSERT `Is it a payment increase decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a payment increase decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a payment increase decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Decision 30 January 2025: pay by 13 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer pay the increase` (`d` 30 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 13 2 2025
#ASSERT `Has the insurer paid the increase in time` (`d` 30 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 13 2 2025) (`d` 20 2 2025) EQUALS `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer paid the increase in time` (`d` 30 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 14 2 2025) (`d` 20 2 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer paid the increase in time` (`d` 30 1 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 20 2 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer paid the increase in time` (`d` 30 1 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `the duty is still open and still in time`

§§ `Part 5 -- return to work assistance`

-- cl 9(1). Arguments: in writing, fixed term, first day, last day.
#ASSERT `Does clause 9 rule out work assistance` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) `any day` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Does clause 9 rule out work assistance` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) `any day` EQUALS TRUE
-- 1 January to 31 March 2025 is 3 months (not less); 1 January to 30 March is less than 3 months.
#ASSERT `Does clause 9 rule out work assistance` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 31 3 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Does clause 9 rule out work assistance` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 30 3 2025) EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 10(1).
#ASSERT `Does clause 10 rule out education or training` TRUE `an NVR registered training organisation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does clause 10 rule out education or training` FALSE `an NVR registered training organisation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Does clause 10 rule out education or training` FALSE `a registered higher education provider` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Does clause 10 rule out education or training` FALSE `another person or body` EQUALS TRUE

-- cll 9(2), 10(2): claim made 1 October 2025: work assistance by 15 October, education or training by 22 October.
#ASSERT `By when must my return to work claim be decided` `a claim for work assistance with a new employer (s 64B)` (`d` 1 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 10 2025
#ASSERT `By when must my return to work claim be decided` `a claim for education or training (s 64C)` (`d` 1 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 22 10 2025
#ASSERT `Has my return to work claim been decided in time` `a claim for work assistance with a new employer (s 64B)` (`d` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`d` 15 10 2025) (`d` 30 10 2025) EQUALS `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has my return to work claim been decided in time` `a claim for work assistance with a new employer (s 64B)` (`d` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`d` 16 10 2025) (`d` 30 10 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has my return to work claim been decided in time` `a claim for education or training (s 64C)` (`d` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`d` 22 10 2025) (`d` 30 10 2025) EQUALS `the duty was kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has my return to work claim been decided in time` `a claim for education or training (s 64C)` (`d` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`d` 23 10 2025) (`d` 30 10 2025) EQUALS `the duty was not kept in time`
#ASSERT `Has my return to work claim been decided in time` `a claim for education or training (s 64C)` (`d` 1 10 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 20 10 2025) EQUALS `the duty is still open and still in time`

§§ `Traces of the regulative rules`

-- cl 8N(1): paid on day 14 fulfils; nothing by day 15 breaches (expect: BREACH by the insurer, the offence reason).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `cl 8N(1) -- the insurer must pay the increase within 14 days of a payment increase decision` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `pay the increase` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#TRACE `cl 8N(1) -- the insurer must pay the increase within 14 days of a payment increase decision` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- cl 8J(2): applied on day 5 fulfils.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `cl 8J(2) -- the application for approval of a PIAWE agreement is to be made within 5 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker or the employer` `apply for approval of the agreement` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
